  "body": "Refs #1448. Part of #1448. Follow-up of #3324.\n\n## Why\n\nThe design of #3324 (`docs/decisions/1448-start-exit-shared.md`, section 2) chooses an operation-level project key for the start and exit picks. The PR of #3324 does not move the storage. The move puts one field on every path variant of `OpParams` and its DTO. More than ten open PRs change `wire_edm.rs` and `wire_edm_dto.rs`, so the move in the same PR conflicts with all of them.\n\nThe accessor `OpParams::path_picks()` hides the storage, so the family slices of #1448 that have a `links` field do not wait for this issue.\n\n## What to do\n\n- Store `camcraft_motion::path_picks::PathPicks` on every path kind.\n- Write the key `picks: { start: [[x, y, z?], ...], exit: [...] }` at the operation level. Write it only when a list is not empty.\n- Read the old keys on load: `links.approach.start_point`, `links.approach.exit_point` and the wire `start`.\n- Keep the digest bytes `0xC7` / `0xC8` for the same values. No contour golden changes.\n- Move `Approach::start_point` / `exit_point` and `WireContourOp.start` into the new field. Change `start_exit_rows.rs`, `start_exit_pick.rs` and the contour planner to read `path_picks()`.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A load test opens a file with the old `links.approach.start_point` key and a file with the old wire `start` key. The picks are the same after the load.\n- Every contour golden and every contour pick test stays green with no change.\n- This merges before the first family slice of #1448 for a kind with no `links` field (Face, turning, plasma).\n",
